{
    "id":  26427,
    "lang":  "en",
    "name":  "LED Strip SCOB 220V 260 LEDs/M 15W/M | 20m Roll | SMD2025 1650Lm/M | IP65 | 10mm | Cut every 5cm",
    "reference":  "SP260D15W-CW-92044",
    "short_description":  "\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003e220V SCOB LED strip (SMD2025 chips), 20 meters,\u003c/strong\u003e is the ideal solution for powerful, uniform, efficient lighting. \u003cstrong\u003eWith 260 LEDs per meter and 15W/m,\u003c/strong\u003e offers high performance of \u003cstrong\u003e1650 lm/m (110 lm/W)\u003c/strong\u003e with a continuous light line and no visible dots. Works directly at 220VAC without transformer. \u003cstrong\u003eTRIAC dimmable\u003c/strong\u003e, IP65 protection, \u003cstrong\u003ecut every 5 cm\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e",
    "description":  "\u003ch2\u003eLED Strip SCOB 220V 260 LED/m 15W/m | 20M Roll | SMD2025 1650Lm/m | IP65 | 10mm | Cut every 5cm\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e220V SCOB LED Strip (SMD2025 chips) 20m. 260 LED/m, 15W/m, 1650Lm/m (110 lm/W). Continuous light line with no visible dots. TRIAC dimmable. IP65. Cut every 5cm.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eWhat is SCOB technology? Differences from SMD and COB\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSCOB (also known as “Spotless COB”) is a hybrid technology between SMD and COB. In a classic \u003cstrong\u003eSMD\u003c/strong\u003e strip the chips are spaced out on the circuit board and, up close, you can see them as individual dots of light. In a \u003cstrong\u003eCOB\u003c/strong\u003e strip the chips are mounted directly on the board under a continuous phosphor layer, giving a uniform line of light, but usually with slightly lower efficiency and more fragility when cutting and handling. A \u003cstrong\u003eSCOB\u003c/strong\u003e strip combines the best of both: it uses very small SMD chips (SMD2025) at a very high density (260 LEDs/m) under a silicone diffusing cover, achieving the continuous, dot-free light of COB while keeping the efficiency (110 lm/W), robustness and easy cutting of SMD.\u003c/p\u003e",
